    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "Hi, I'm trying to train a BPE tokenizer on Nemotron-CC (https://data.commoncrawl.org/contrib/Nemotron/Nemotron-CC/index.html) and I'm running into memory issues when scaling up the training data. I'm not too familiar with tokenizer training, but from what I gathered, it is generally considered that the more training data the better. With that being said, I'm quickly running out of memory when training on more than 100GB (zstd compressed) text on a vocab size of 131k, exceeding the 750GB RAM that are available.\n\nNow I'm wondering whether I'm doing something wrong/suboptimally, or whether BPE inherently requires this much memory, or whether the `tokenizers` library is simply not built for this amount of data.\n\nFor reference, here's the spirit of what I'm doing. I'm loading and decompressing the JSONLs on-the-fly, using `tokenizer.train_from_iterator` to feed line by line:\n\n```py\n\ndef load_file(input_path, quiet=True):\n    docs = []\n    with open(input_path, 'rb') as f:\n        byte_data = f.read()\n        try:\n            data = zstd.decompress(byte_data)\n            data = data.decode(\"utf-8\")\n            for line in data.splitlines():\n                docs.append(json.loads(line.rstrip(\"\\n|\\r\")))\n        except zstd.Error as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Error decompressing {input_path}\")\n    if not quiet:\n        print(\"Loaded {} records from {}\".format(len(data), input_path))\n    return docs\n\n\ndef json_iterator(all_jsonls, text_key=\"text\"):\n    for j in all_jsonls:\n        for doc in load_file(j):\n            yield doc[text_key]\n\n...\n\ntokenizer.pre_tokenizer = pre_tokenizers.Sequence([\n  pre_tokenizers.Split(\n    Regex(r\"[^\\r\\n\\p{L}\\p{N}]?[\\p{L}]+|\\p{N}{1,3}| ?[^\\s\\p{L}\\p{N}]+[\\r\\n]*|\\s*[\\r\\n]+|\\s+(?!\\S)|\\s+\"),\n    behavior=\"isolated\",\n    invert=False\n  ),\n  pre_tokenizers.ByteLevel(add_prefix_space=False, trim_offsets=True, use_regex=False),\n])\ntokenizer.normalizer = normalizers.NFC()\n\n...\n\ntrainer = trainers.BpeTrainer(vocab_size=131_072)\ntokenizer.train_from_iterator(json_iterator(all_jsonls), trainer, length=total_lines)\n```",
    "closed_at": "2025-07-08T10:09:23Z",
